# @facet/rust/materialize — the Rust altitude's recognitive turn
# realisation.
#
# The metalogue-turn-pair recognition (2026-06-10, Alex → Mara via
# Reed): `@facet/metalogue` declares the substrate-pull-correct
# ground for the AST altitude's metalogue. The shim direction
# (substrate utters → species emits) is realised PER-SPECIES at
# `@facet/X/macro` shards (cf. `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror`).
# The recognitive direction (species utters → substrate
# recognises) is realised PER-SPECIES at `@facet/X/materialize`
# shards — this file is the Rust-altitude binding.
#
# Why under `@facet/rust` (not a new `@facet/materialize` family or
# the prior `@mirror/realisation` home): per
# docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md §2 substrate-pull check,
# `@facet/X` species carry per-language altitude grammars. The
# metalogue/materialize recognition sub-prism IS-A part of the
# language altitude (the way `@facet/rust/macro` IS-A part of
# `@facet/rust`, the way `@facet/rust/cargo` IS-A part of
# `@facet/rust`), not a sibling family. The classifier's INPUT is
# a `code/rust.ast`; the home pulls to the species altitude. Path-
# namespace property per
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: this file at
# `shards/code/rust/materialize.mirror` declares
# `@facet/rust/materialize`. The path IS the declaration.
#
# === Inheritance from @facet/metalogue/materialize ===
#
# The recognitive turn's contract (`classify` /
# `is_materialisable` / `target_altitude` action signatures, the
# `materialised_file` + `partition` carriers, the four laws) is
# declared ONCE at `shards/code/metalogue/materialize.mirror`.
# This shard inherits via `in @facet/metalogue/materialize` per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]'s `<=` mechanism
# (`in @X` is the canonical import-and-inherit form). The action
# signatures below specialise the ground's parametric
# `declaration` carrier to a Rust-AST-parsed declaration; the
# laws come for free from the ground's `requires` clauses.
#
# === The 30th-instance training set, lifted ===
#
# Per the prior `shards/mirror/realisation.mirror` §"The training
# set" (now retired; the narrative lifts to the new home with
# minor edits to reflect the per-species binding):
#
# The 29 substrate-pull recognitions logged through 2026-06-08 in
# `roadmap/2026-06-08-rug-pull.md` §5 are the labelled (Rust-code-
# shape, substrate-altitude) pairs the per-species body's match
# table walks. Each row is one `classify()` training example for
# the Rust-altitude binding:
#
#   #16 lift (foundational, not zoom)               -> @prism
#   #18 eigensheaf (spectral decomposition)         -> @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian
#   #19 five operations are Hodge primitives        -> @prism
#   #20 eigenspace (composition foundation)         -> @mirror/spectral/composition
#   #21 prophecy (derive fractures from topology)   -> @kintsugi/fracture/predicate
#   #22 score family root                            -> @mirror/spectral/score
#   #23 glass IS lens (four names, one primitive)    -> @mirror/lens + @mirror/loss
#   #24 oscillate_witness (next-oscillation)         -> @kintsugi/oscillate
#   #25 morphism_context (per-candidate slice)       -> @kintsugi/morphism
#   #26 shift(oid, T) typed-capability primitive     -> @mirror/spectral/portal
#   #27 template render (one operation, many uses)   -> @facet/mirror
#   #28 "path was already half-built" (json lift)    -> @mirror/data
#   #29 "presence IS the signal" (SCM_RIGHTS)        -> @mirror/spectral/portal
#
# The discriminator's body (when it lands; T22 MVP at
# `bootstrap/src/realisation.rs` is the current boundary-Rust
# realisation, will lift to substrate-source through
# kintsugi-on-Rust when the consumer pulls) reads the
# `code/rust.ast` and walks the family roster: does this file's
# structural shape match `@mirror/lens`'s family? `@mirror/loss`'s?
# `@facet/mirror`'s? The 29 prior recognitions teach the
# discriminator what "shape-match" means at each altitude.
#
# === The carrier vs the verdict (two surfaces) ===
#
# Per the ground's §"The carrier vs the verdict": the full
# `materialised_file` record is consumed by cross-wall kintsugi
# (T22+) to produce fracture proposals; the binary `is_materialisable`
# verdict is consumed by mosaic's `settle_on` and the audition
# altitude (`@mirror/spectral/audition`); the `target_altitude`
# projection is consumed by per-altitude fracture diffing. Three
# readers, three projections, one carrier — at this altitude the
# carrier IS the Rust-altitude binding of the recognitive verdict.
#
# === Five-op block ===
#
# Per the in-flight depth-2 recognition (#46 pending, glass for
# depth-≥1 declarations): this sub-prism uses `glass` since it is
# depth-2 (`@facet/rust` is depth-1; `@facet/rust/materialize` is
# depth-2). Cf. `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror`'s depth-2 `prism`
# declaration that the sweep will lift; this new shard uses the
# new vocabulary from birth.
glass @facet/rust/materialize {
  focus materialize
  project materialize
  split materialize
  shift materialize
  settle materialize
}

# === Rust-altitude binding ===
#
# The three action signatures from `@facet/metalogue/materialize`
# (universal contract) bind here to `code/rust.ast` as the
# species AST type. The contract and laws inherit from the ground
# via `in @facet/metalogue/materialize`; this shard's job is the
# per-altitude binding plus the realisation cascade.
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: bodies are `\` until a
# consumer-pull tick. The boundary-Rust realisation at
# `bootstrap/src/realisation.rs` (T22 MVP, the hardcoded
# basename match table) IS the current consumer; that file
# lifts to substrate-source when the discriminator's body
# discharges through kintsugi-on-Rust at T22+.

# `classify(d) -> materialised_file` — the recognitive primitive
# for Rust forms. Reads a `code/rust.ast`-parsed declaration;
# emits the full materialised_file record (path / partition /
# target / verdict). Body discharges by walking the AST against
# the family roster (@io, @facet/mirror, @mirror/lens,
# @mirror/loss, @mirror/data, @mirror/spectral,
# @epistemologic/math/*) and pattern-matching the file's
# structural shape against each altitude's declared grammar. The
# 29 substrate-pull recognitions are the training set.
classify(d: declaration) -> materialised_file { \ }

# `is_materialisable(d) -> verdict` — the binary projection at
# the Rust altitude. Reads `classify(d).verdict` projected
# through the partition; clear when materialisable at substrate
# OR clear-permanent-@io; opaque when mixed.
is_materialisable(d: declaration) -> verdict { \ }

# `target_altitude(d) -> ref` — the targeting projection at the
# Rust altitude. Reads `classify(d).target`; consumed directly
# by cross-wall kintsugi to produce the first fracture proposal
# against the target altitude's grammar.
target_altitude(d: declaration) -> ref { \ }

# === Alex 2026-08-21 reframe: parse-dep-tree = autopoietic litmus ===
#
# Alex 2026-08-21 in-transcript reframe (post-HALT Phase 4 scoping):
# *"The litmus test is that mirror can parse the totality of mirror's
# own dependency tree in rust. Does that help? Think of mirror as a loop
# with `in` and `out`s and each increment widens the autopoietic
# surface that the loop can cover."*
#
# Reed pre-reframe scope drift: had been authoring forward-projection
# `𝔕_rust` (substrate → source-emit fixed-point) per Rec #91 amendment
# §5a Theorem 5a.1 discharge. That direction requires substantial multi-
# week AST substrate authoring (Rust grammar 2-3× Erlang precedent). NOT
# a /loop-cadence discharge.
#
# Alex-corrected scope: the LITMUS is the REVERSE direction (`𝔛_rust`
# per Rec #91 amendment §5a.1) — mirror READS its own rust/ dep tree +
# represents as substrate. Each increment widens the autopoietic
# surface the loop can cover. Progressive expansion, not big-bang.
#
# === increment plan (Reed post-reframe) ===
#
# I1: mirror invokes `cargo metadata --format-version 1 --manifest-path
#     rust/Cargo.toml` (existing phone.rs::spawn_cargo_build primitive
#     adapted for metadata subcommand); parses JSON output (existing
#     wire.rs @data/json primitive); represents workspace members
#     (fractal + matrix + roomba + spectral + tests + main) as substrate
#     splinters at @mirror/store altitude. Empirical fire: mirror KNOWS
#     its own workspace-member set. Autopoietic surface increment 1.
#
# I2: For each workspace member, parse its Cargo.toml [dependencies]
#     from cargo metadata JSON output; represent dep-graph edges as
#     substrate splinters. Empirical: mirror KNOWS its own inter-crate
#     dep graph (main → {fractal, matrix, spectral, roomba, prismqueer};
#     matrix → {fractal, prismqueer}; etc.). Autopoietic surface
#     increment 2.
#
# I3: For each rust/**/src/**/*.rs file, extract `use` statements via
#     grep-level parsing (not full Rust AST); represent intra-crate
#     file-level dep graph as substrate splinters. Empirical: mirror
#     KNOWS its own module-import structure. Autopoietic surface
#     increment 3.
#
# I4: Extend to full Rust AST parsing via shelling to `rustc --emit
#     dep-info` or `cargo-syn` (external tool composition); represent
#     AST-level dep-graph as substrate. Empirical: TOTALITY of dep tree
#     parsed per Alex litmus. Autopoietic surface increment 4.
#
# === substrate-honest scope for I1-I4 ===
#
# I1 + I2 are shell-out-plus-JSON-parse compositions. Landed rust/
# primitives (phone.rs::spawn_cargo_build + wire.rs::parse) suffice;
# NO new rust/ primitive authoring per Alex 2026-08-05 rust-delivers-
# primitives / substrate-delivers-composition HARD RULE. Just wire
# `mirror facet materialize` CLI verb at rust/src/main.rs dispatching
# to shard-body composition via apply_h::act.
#
# I3 requires small addition: grep-level `use`-statement extraction
# (regex against file bytes; no full Rust parser). Composition-shard
# body over @io/fs.read + string manipulation primitives.
#
# I4 requires substantial external-tool composition (rustc / cargo-syn)
# OR full Rust parser as substrate authoring. Defer to future arc.
#
# === body actions extension for cargo-metadata litmus ===
#
# The classify() action above signatures over `code/rust.ast` (parsed-
# declaration input). For I1-I2 (cargo metadata parsing), the input is
# `manifest_ref` (a Cargo.toml file path) and the output is a workspace-
# representation splinter. Different arity from classify(d). Extension:

# `classify_workspace(manifest: ref) -> workspace_splinter` — the
# parse-workspace action for I1. Reads a Cargo.toml manifest ref;
# invokes `cargo metadata --format-version 1 --manifest-path
# <manifest>`; parses JSON via wire.rs; represents workspace members
# as splinter graph at @mirror/store altitude. Body discharges when
# rust/ CLI verb `mirror facet materialize workspace <manifest>` is
# wired (I1 empirical fire tick).
classify_workspace(manifest: ref) -> workspace_splinter { \ }

# `classify_dependency_tree(root: ref) -> dep_graph_splinter` — the
# parse-dep-tree action for I2. Reads a workspace-root Cargo.toml
# ref; parses cargo metadata output; represents inter-crate dep-
# graph as content-addressed splinter graph. Body discharges when
# I2 empirical fire is authored.
classify_dependency_tree(root: ref) -> dep_graph_splinter { \ }

# `classify_use_graph(src_root: ref) -> module_import_splinter` — the
# parse-use-statements action for I3. Reads rust/**/src/**/*.rs files;
# extracts `use` statements via grep-level regex (no full Rust
# parser); represents intra-crate module-import structure as splinter
# graph. Body discharges when I3 empirical fire is authored.

# === Citations + cascade context ===
#
